# domain
- Viktor is an AI employee reachable at https://api.viktor.com (staging https://staging.viktor.test) through an OpenAI Chat Completions and Responses wire at <host>/api/compat/v1, an Anthropic Messages wire at <host>/api/compat, a hosted stateless Streamable-HTTP MCP server at <host>/mcp, and a native async REST API at <host>/api/public/v1
- a Core is the per-language shared package (TS `packages/core`, Py `python/core`) that owns the Viktor client, canonical message model, streaming parsing, error classification, and fixtures
- an Adapter is a thin per-framework package that depends on one Core and one upstream framework and only converts types and registers with the framework
- a RoutedToolId is a Viktor tool-call id of the form call_vk1_<thread>_<c|t|b>_<suffix> (toolu_vk1_… on the Anthropic wire) that embeds the durable thread id
- a Fixture is a recorded wire exchange (request, response or SSE frames) replayed in unit tests without network
- a LiveContractTest is a test that runs against the real Viktor API when VIKTOR_API_KEY is set and is skipped otherwise

# core/client
- label: the client reads VIKTOR_API_KEY and VIKTOR_BASE_URL (default https://api.viktor.com) from the environment when not given explicitly
  command: scripts/vt.sh packages/core test/core.test.ts 'reads VIKTOR_API_KEY and VIKTOR_BASE_URL'
  tags: [implemented, core-ts]
- label: the client sends the key as `Authorization: Bearer` and always sends model `viktor`
  command: scripts/vt.sh packages/core test/core.test.ts 'sends bearer auth, forces model viktor'
  tags: [implemented, core-ts]
- the client exposes chat completions (sync and streaming), responses (sync and streaming), anthropic messages (sync and streaming), and list models @spec
- the client interface is narrow enough to be re-implemented on top of the Viktor SDK without changing any adapter @spec

# core/continuation
- label: tool-call ids from Viktor are passed through unchanged in both directions so a follow-up with trailing tool results resumes the durable thread
  command: scripts/vt.sh packages/core test/core.test.ts 'sends tool results with the routed id unchanged'
  tags: [implemented, core-ts]
- label: the core exposes a helper that extracts the Viktor thread id from a RoutedToolId or a Responses response id, returning null for non-routed ids
  command: scripts/vt.sh packages/core test/core.test.ts 'extracts the thread id'
  tags: [implemented, core-ts]
- tool declarations are re-sent on every request including resume turns @spec

# core/streaming
- label: the Chat Completions SSE parser assembles fragmented tool-call arguments by index and yields text deltas, tool calls, finish reason, and optional usage
  command: scripts/vt.sh packages/core test/core.test.ts 'assembles fragmented tool-call arguments'
  tags: [implemented, core-ts]
- label: an in-stream `{"error":…}` data frame on the Chat Completions wire is surfaced as a typed ViktorRunFailedError carrying the worker message, not as a normal end of stream
  command: scripts/vt.sh packages/core test/core.test.ts 'in-stream error frame'
  tags: [implemented, core-ts]
- a Responses `response.failed` event and an Anthropic `event: error` are surfaced as ViktorRunFailedError and the trailing `[Stream error: …]` text is dropped @spec
- label: keep-alive comment lines are ignored by the parser and never surface as content
  command: scripts/vt.sh packages/core test/core.test.ts 'ignores keep-alive comments'
  tags: [implemented, core-ts]

